n contain file attachments included in chat messages. The vulnerability was partially patched in version 3.3.3.',7.5,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N',3.6,3.9,'kainex','wise_chat',4),('CVE-2024-13617','2025-03-25','2025-06-20','Analyzed','The aoa-downloadable WordPress plugin through 0.1.0 doesn\'t validate a parameter in its download function, allowing unauthenticated attackers to download arbitrary files from the server',8.6,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N',4.0,3.9,'osteopathic','downloadable_by_american_osteopathic_association',1),('CVE-2024-13618','2025-03-25','2025-06-20','Analyzed','The aoa-downloadable WordPress plugin through 0.1.0 lacks authorization and authentication for requests to its download.php endpoint, allowing unauthenticated visitors to make requests to arbitrary URLs.',7.2,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N',2.7,3.9,'osteopathic','downloadable_by_american_osteopathic_association',1),('CVE-2024-13622','2025-02-18','2025-03-17','Analyzed','The File Uploads Addon for WooCommerce plugin for WordPress is vulnerable to Sensitive Information Exposure in all versions up to, and including, 1.7.1 via the \'uploads\' directory. This makes it possible for unauthenticated attackers to extract sensitive data stored insecurely in the /wp-content/uploads directory which can contain file attachments uploaded by customers.',7.5,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N',3.6,3.9,'imaginate-solutions','file_uploads_addon_for_woocommerce',3),('CVE-2024-13624','2025-02-26','2025-05-15','Analyzed','The WPMovieLibrary WordPress plugin through 2.1.4.8 does not sanitise and escape a parameter before outputting it back in the page, leading to a Reflected Cross-Site Scripting which could be used against high privilege users such as admin.',7.1,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:L',3.7,2.8,'caercam','wpmovielibrary',1),('CVE-2024-13625','2025-02-17','2025