y allow an authenticated user to potentially enable escalation of privilege via local access.',7.9,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:C/C:N/I:H/A:H',5.8,1.5,'','',2),('CVE-2024-21815','2024-03-05','2025-02-10','Analyzed',' Insufficiently protected credentials (CWE-522) for third party DVR integrations to the Command Centre Server are accessible to authenticated but unprivileged users.   This issue affects: Gallagher Command Centre 9.00 prior to vEL9.00.1774 (MR2), 8.90 prior to vEL8.90.1751 (MR3), 8.80 prior to vEL8.80.1526 (MR4), 8.70 prior to vEL8.70.2526 (MR6),  all version of 8.60 and prior.    ',9.1,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:L/A:L',5.3,3.1,'gallagher','command_centre',2),('CVE-2024-21820','2024-11-13','2024-11-15','Awaiting Analysis','Incorrect default permissions in some Intel(R) Xeon(R) processor memory controller configurations when using Intel(R) SGX may allow a privileged user to potentially enable escalation of privilege via local access.',7.2,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:N',5.8,0.8,'','',1),('CVE-2024-21821','2024-01-11','2025-06-17','Modified','Multiple TP-LINK products allow a network-adjacent authenticated attacker with access to the product from the LAN port or Wi-Fi to execute arbitrary OS commands.',8.0,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.1,'tp-link','archer_axe75, archer_ax5400, archer_ax5400_firmware, archer_axe75_firmware, archer_ax3000',10),('CVE-2024-21823','2024-05-16','2024-11-21','Awaiting Analysis','Hardware logic with insecure de-synchronization in Intel(R) DSA and Intel(R) IAA for some Intel(R) 4th or 5th generation Xeon(R) processors may allow an authorized user to potentially enable escalation of privilege local access',7.5,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:H/A:H',5.8,1.1,'','',8),('CVE-2024-21825','2024-02-26','2025-02-12','Analyzed','A heap-based buffer overflow vulnerability exists in the GGUF library GGUF_TYPE_