ility could allow a remote attacker to send a specially crafted URL to an authenticated user and steal their session cookie credentials.',8.2,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:L/A:N',4.7,2.8,'ajaysharma','cups_easy',2),('CVE-2024-23897','2024-01-24','2024-12-20','Analyzed','Jenkins 2.441 and earlier, LTS 2.426.2 and earlier does not disable a feature of its CLI command parser that replaces an \'@\' character followed by a file path in an argument with the file\'s contents, allowing unauthenticated attackers to read arbitrary files on the Jenkins controller file system.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'jenkins','jenkins',11),('CVE-2024-23898','2024-01-24','2025-06-20','Modified','Jenkins 2.217 through 2.441 (both inclusive), LTS 2.222.1 through 2.426.2 (both inclusive) does not perform origin validation of requests made through the CLI WebSocket endpoint, resulting in a cross-site WebSocket hijacking (CSWSH) vulnerability, allowing attackers to execute CLI commands on the Jenkins controller.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'jenkins','jenkins',6),('CVE-2024-2390','2024-03-18','2024-11-21','Awaiting Analysis',' As a part of Tenable’s vulnerability disclosure program, a vulnerability in a Nessus plugin was identified and reported. This vulnerability could allow a malicious actor with sufficient permissions on a scan target to place a binary in a specific filesystem location, and abuse the impacted plugin in order to escalate privileges.  ',7.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.8,'','',2),('CVE-2024-23904','2024-01-24','2025-06-20','Modified','Jenkins Log Command Plugin 1.0.2 and earlier does not disable a feature of its command parser that replaces an \'@\' character followed by a file path in an argument with the file\'s contents, allowing unauthenticated attackers to read content from arbitrary files on the Jenkins controller file system.',7.5,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N',3.6,3.9,'jenkins','log_command',4),('CVE-2024-23910','2024-02-28','2025-04-22','Modified','Cross-site request forgery (CSRF) vulnerability in ELECOM wireless LAN routers and wireless LAN repeater allows a remote unauthenticated attacker to hijack the authentication of administrators and to perform unintended operations to the affected product. Note that WMC-X1800GST-B and WSC-X1800GS-B are also included in e-Mesh Starter Kit \"WMC-2LX-B\".',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'elecom','wrc-1167gs2h-b, wrc-1167gst2, wmc-x1800gst-b, wrc-2533gs2v-b, wrc-2533gs2-w',4),('CVE-2024-23911','2024-04-15','2025-06-30','Analyzed','Out-of-bounds read vulnerability caused by improper checking of the option length values in IPv6 NDP packets exists in Cente middleware TCP/IP Network Series, which may allow an unauthenticated attacker to stop the device operations by sending a specially crafted packet.',7.5,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H',3.6,3.9,'nxtech','cente_ipv6_snmpv2, cente_ipv6_snmpv3, cente_ipv6',4),('CVE-2024-23917','2024-02-06','2024-11-21','Modified','In JetBrains TeamCity before 2023.11.3 authentication bypass leading to RCE was possible',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'jetbrains','teamcity',2),('CVE-2024-23918','2024-11-13','2024-11-15','Awaiting Analysis','Improper conditions check in some Intel(R) Xeon(R) processor memory controller configurations when using Intel(R) SGX may allow a privileged user to potentially enable escalation of privilege via local access.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H',6.0,2.0,'','',1),('CVE-2024-23920','2025-01-31','2025-07-01','Modified','This vulnerability allows network-adjacent attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of ChargePoint Home Flex charging stations. Authentication is not required to exploit this vulnerability.  The specific flaw exists within the onboardee module. The issue results from improper access control. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of root.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'chargepoint','home_flex_nema_14-50_plug_firmware, home_flex_hardwired_firmware, home_flex_hardwired, home_flex_nema_6-50_plug, home_flex_nema_6-50_plug_firmware',1),('CVE-2024-23921','2025-01-31','2025-07-01','Modified','This vulnerability allows network-adjacent attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of ChargePoint Home Flex charging stations. Authentication is not required to exploit this vulnerability.  The specific flaw exists within the wlanapp module. The issue results from the lack of proper validation of a user-supplied string before using it to execute a system call. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of root.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'chargepoint','home_flex_nema_14-50_plug_firmware, home_flex_hardwired_firmware, home_flex_hardwired, home_flex_nema_6-50_plug, home_flex_nema_6-50_plug_firmware',1),('CVE-2024-23923','2024-09-28','2024-10-03','Analyzed','Alpine Halo9 prh_l2_sar_data_ind Use-After-Free Remote Code Execution Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows network-adjacent attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Alpine Halo9 devices. Authentication is not required to exploit this vulnerability.  The specific flaw exists within the prh_l2_sar_data_ind function. The issue results from the lack of validating the existence of an object prior to performing operations on the object. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of root.  Was ZDI-CAN-22945',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'alpsalpine','ilx-f509_firmware, ilx-f509',1),('CVE-2024-23929','2025-01-31','2025-07-01','Modified','This vulnerability allows network-adjacent attackers to create arbitrary files on affected installations of Pioneer DMH-WT7600NEX devices. Although authentication is required to exploit this vulnerability, the existing authentication mechanism can be bypassed.  The specific flaw exists within the telematics functionality. The issue results from the lack of proper validation of a user-supplied path prior to using it in file operations. An attacker can leverage this in conjunction with other vulnerabilities to execute arbitrary code in the context of root.',7.3,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H',5.2,2.1,'pioneer','dmh-wt7600nex_firmware, dmh-wt7600nex',2),('CVE-2024-23934','2024-09-23','2024-09-26','Awaiting Analysis','Sony XAV-AX5500 WMV/ASF Parsing Stack-based Buffer Overflow Remote Code Execution Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Sony XAV-AX5500 devices. User interaction is required to exploit this vulnerability in that the target must visit a malicious page or open a malicious file.  The specific flaw exists within the parsing of WMV/ASF files. A crafted Extended Content Description Object in a WMV media file can trigger an overflow of a fixed-length stack-based buffer. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of the device.  . Was ZDI-CAN-22994.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'','',2),('CVE-2024-23935','2024-09-28','2024-10-03','Analyzed','Alpine Halo9 DecodeUTF7 Stack-based Buffer Overflow Remote Code Execution Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows network-adjacent attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Alpine Halo9 devices. An attacker must first obtain the ability to pair a malicious Bluetooth device with the target system in order to exploit this vulnerability.  The specific flaw exists within the DecodeUTF7 function. The issue results from the lack of proper validation of the length of user-supplied data prior to copying it to a stack-based buffer. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of root.  Was ZDI-CAN-23249',8.0,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.1,'alpsalpine','ilx-f509_firmware, ilx-f509',1),('CVE-2024-23938','2024-09-28','2024-10-03','Analyzed','Silicon Labs Gecko OS Debug Interface Stack-based Buffer Overflow Remote Code Execution Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows network-adjacent attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Silicon Labs Gecko OS. Authentication is not required to exploit this vulnerability.  The specific flaw exists within the debug interface. The issue results from the lack of proper validation of the length of user-supplied data prior to copying it to a stack-based buffer. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of the device.  Was ZDI-CAN-23184',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'silabs','gecko_os',2),('CVE-2024-23940','2024-01-29','2025-05-29','Modified','Trend Micro uiAirSupport, included in the Trend Micro Security 2023 family of consumer products, version 6.0.2092 and below is vulnerable to a DLL hijacking/proxying vulnerability, which if exploited could allow an attacker to impersonate and modify a library to execute code on the system and ultimately escalate privileges on an affected system.',7.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.8,'microsoft, trendmicro','windows, premium_security, antivirus_+_security, maximum_security, internet_security',6),('CVE-2024-23942','2025-03-18','2025-08-20','Awaiting Analysis','A local user may find a configuration file on the client workstation with unencrypted sensitive data. This allows an attacker to impersonate the device or prevent the device from accessing the cloud portal which leads to a DoS.',7.1,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H',5.2,1.8,'','',1),('CVE-2024-23943','2025-03-18','2025-03-18','Awaiting Analysis','An unauthenticated remote attacker can gain access to the cloud API due to a lack of authentication for a critical function in the affected devices. Availability is not affected.',9.1,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N',5.2,3.9,'','',1),('CVE-2024-23947','2024-05-28','2025-02-12','Analyzed','Multiple improper array index validation vulnerabilities exist in the readMSH functionality of libigl v2.5.0. A specially crafted .msh file can lead to an out-of-bounds write. An attacker can provide a malicious file to trigger this vulnerability.This vulnerability concerns the `igl::MshLoader::parse_nodes` function while handling a `binary` `.msh` file.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'libigl','libigl',4),('CVE-2024-23948','2024-05-28','2025-02-12','Analyzed','Multiple improper array index validation vulnerabilities exist in the readMSH functionality of libigl v2.5.0. A specially crafted .msh file can lead to an out-of-bounds write. An attacker can provide a malicious file to trigger this vulnerability.This vulnerability concerns the `igl::MshLoader::parse_nodes` function while handling an `ascii`.msh` file.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'libigl','libigl',4),('CVE-2024-23949','2024-05-28','2025-02-12','Analyzed','Multiple improper array index validation vulnerabilities exist in the readMSH functionality of libigl v2.5.0. A specially crafted .msh file can lead to an out-of-bounds write. An attacker can provide a malicious file to trigger this vulnerability.This vulnerability concerns the `igl::MshLoader::parse_node_field` function while handling an `ascii`.msh` file.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'libigl','libigl',4),('CVE-2024-2395','2024-03-12','2025-01-22','Analyzed','The Bulgarisation for WooCommerce plugin for WordPress is vulnerable to Cross-Site Request Forgery in all versions up to, and including, 3.0.14. This is due to missing or incorrect nonce validation on several functions. This makes it possible for unauthenticated attackers to generate and delete labels via a forged request granted they can trick a site administrator into performing an action such as clicking on a link.',7.3,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L',3.4,3.9,'autopolis','bulgarisation_for_woocommerce',4),('CVE-2024-23950','2024-05-28','2025-02-12','Analyzed','Multiple improper array index validation vulnerabilities exist in the readMSH functionality of libigl v2.5.0. A specially crafted .msh file can lead to an out-of-bounds write. An attacker can provide a malicious file to trigger this vulnerability.This vulnerability concerns the `igl::MshLoader::parse_element_field` function while handling an `binary`.msh` file.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'libigl','libigl',4),('CVE-2024-23951','2024-05-28','2025-02-12','Analyzed','Multiple improper array index validation vulnerabilities exist in the readMSH functionality of libigl v2.5.0. A specially crafted .msh file can lead to an out-of-bounds write. An attacker can provide a malicious file to trigger this vulnerability.This vulnerability concerns the `igl::MshLoader::parse_element_field` function while handling an `ascii`.msh` file.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'libigl','libigl',4),('CVE-2024-23957','2024-09-28','2024-10-03','Analyzed','Autel MaxiCharger AC Elite Business C50 DLB_HostHeartBeat Stack-based Buffer Overflow Remote Code Execution Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows network-adjacent attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Autel MaxiCharger AC Elite Business C50 charging stations. Authentication is not required to exploit this vulnerability.  The specific flaw exists within the DLB_HostHeartBeat handler of the DLB protocol implementation. When parsing an AES key, the process does not properly validate the length of user-supplied data prior to copying it to a fixed-length stack-based buffer. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of the device.  Was ZDI-CAN-23241',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'autel','maxicharger_ac_elite_business_c50_firmware, maxicharger_ac_elite_business_c50',1),('CVE-2024-23959','2024-09-28','2024-10-03','Analyzed','Autel MaxiCharger AC Elite Business C50 BLE AppChargingControl Stack-based Buffer Overflow Remote Code Execution Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows network-adjacent attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Autel MaxiCharger AC Elite Business C50 charging stations. Although authentication is required to exploit this vulnerability, the existing authentication mechanism can be bypassed.  The specific flaw exists within the handling of the AppChargingControl BLE command. The issue results from the lack of proper validation of the length of user-supplied data prior to copying it to a fixed-length stack-based buffer. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of the device.  Was ZDI-CAN-23194',8.0,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.1,'autel','maxicharger_ac_elite_business_c50_firmware, maxicharger_ac_elite_business_c50',1),('CVE-2024-23963','2025-01-31','2025-08-12','Analyzed','This vulnerability allows network-adjacent attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Alpine Halo9 devices. An attacker must first obtain the ability to pair a malicious Bluetooth device with the target system in order to exploit this vulnerability.  The specific flaw exists within the PBAP_DecodeVCARD function. The issue results from the lack of proper validation of the length of user-supplied data prior to copying it to a stack-based buffer. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of root.',8.0,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.1,'alpsalpine','ilx-f509_firmware, ilx-f509',1),('CVE-2024-23967','2024-09-28','2024-10-03','Analyzed','Autel MaxiCharger AC Elite Business C50 WebSocket Base64 Decoding Stack-based Buffer Overflow Remote Code Execution Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows network-adjacent attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Autel MaxiCharger AC Elite Business C50 chargers. Although authentication is required to exploit this vulnerability, the existing authentication mechanism can be bypassed.  The specific flaw exists within the handling of base64-encoded data within WebSocket messages. The issue results from the lack of proper validation of the length of user-supplied data prior to copying it to a fixed-length stack-based buffer. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of the device.  Was ZDI-CAN-23230',8.0,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.1,'autel','maxicharger_ac_elite_business_c50_firmware, maxicharger_ac_elite_business_c50',1),('CVE-2024-23968','2025-01-31','2025-06-30','Modified','This vulnerability allows network-adjacent attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of ChargePoint Home Flex charging stations. Authentication is not required to exploit this vulnerability.  The specific flaw exists within the SrvrToSmSetAutoChnlListMsg function. The issue results from the lack of proper validation of the length of user-supplied data prior to copying it to a fixed-length stack-based buffer. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of root.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'chargepoint','home_flex_nema_14-50_plug_firmware, home_flex_hardwired_firmware, home_flex_hardwired, home_flex_nema_6-50_plug, home_flex_nema_6-50_plug_firmware',1),('CVE-2024-23969','2025-01