.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'tenda','ac9, ac9_firmware',2),('CVE-2024-2575','2024-03-18','2025-02-20','Analyzed','A vulnerability, which was classified as critical, has been found in SourceCodester Employee Task Management System 1.0. Affected by this issue is some unknown functionality of the file /task-details.php. The manipulation of the argument task_id leads to authorization bypass. The attack may be launched remotely. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. VDB-257078 is the identifier assigned to this vulnerability.',7.3,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L',3.4,3.9,'oretnom23','employee_task_management_system',6),('CVE-2024-25751','2024-02-26','2025-03-13','Analyzed','A Stack Based Buffer Overflow vulnerability in Tenda AC9 v.3.0 with firmware version v.15.03.06.42_multi allows a remote attacker to execute arbitrary code via the fromSetSysTime function.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'tenda','ac9, ac9_firmware',2),('CVE-2024-25753','2024-02-22','2025-03-13','Analyzed','Stack Based Buffer Overflow vulnerability in Tenda AC9 v.3.0 with firmware version v.15.03.06.42_multi allows a remote attacker to execute arbitrary code via the formSetDeviceName function.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'tenda','ac9, ac9_firmware',2),('CVE-2024-25756','2024-02-22','2025-03-13','Analyzed','A Stack Based Buffer Overflow vulnerability in Tenda AC9 v.3.0 with firmware version v.15.03.06.42_multi allows a remote attacker to execute arbitrary code via the formWifiBasicSet function.',8.0,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.1,'tenda','ac9, ac9_firmware',2),('CVE-2024-2576','2024-03-18','2025-02-20','Analyzed','A vulnerability, which was classified as critical, was found in SourceCodester Employee Task Management System 1.0. This affects an unknown part of the file /update-admin.php. The manipulation of the argument admin_id leads to authorization bypass. It is possible to initiate the attack remotely. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. The associated identifier of this vulnerability is VDB-257079.',7.3,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L',3.4,3.9,'oretnom23','employee_task_management_system',6),('CVE-2024-25768','2024-02-26','2025-05-01','Analyzed','OpenDMARC 1.4.2 contains a null pointer dereference vulnerability in /OpenDMARC/libopendmarc/opendmarc_policy.c.',7.5,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H',3.6,3.9,'trusteddomain','opendmarc',2),('CVE-2024-2577','2024-03-18','2025-02-20','Analyzed','A vulnerability has been found in SourceCodester Employee Task Management System 1.0 and classified as critical. This vulnerability affects unknown code of the file /update-employee.php. The manipulation of the argument admin_id leads to authorization bypass. The attack can be initiated remotely. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. The identifier of this vulnerability is VDB-257080.',7.3,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L',3.4,3.9,'oretnom23','employee_task_management_system',6),('CVE-2024-25802','2024-02-22','2025-02-14','Analyzed','SKINsoft S-Museum 7.02.3 allows Unrestricted File Upload via the Add Media function. Unlike in CVE-2024-25801, the attack payload is the file content.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'skinsoft','s-museum',2),('CVE-2024-25808','2024-03-22','2025-05-28','Analyzed','Cross-site Request Forgery (CSRF) vulnerability in Lychee version 3.1.6, allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary code via the create new album function.',8.3,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:L',5.5,2.8,'lycheeorg','lychee',2),('CVE-2024-2581','2024-03-18','2025-01-22','Analyzed','A vulnerability was found in Tenda AC10 16.03.10.13 and classified as critical. This issue affects the function fromSetRouteStatic of the file /goform/SetStaticRouteCfg. The manipulation of the argument list leads to stack-based buffer overflow. The attack may be initiated remotely. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. The identifier VDB-257081 was assigned to this vulnerability.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'tenda','ac10, ac10_firmware',6),('CVE-2024-25817','2024-03-06','2025-01-15','Analyzed','Buffer Overflow vulnerability in eza before version 0.18.2, allows local attackers to execute arbitrary code via the .git/HEAD, .git/refs, and .git/objects components.',7.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.8,'eza.rock','eza',4),('CVE-2024-25825','2024-10-09','2024-10-11','Awaiting Analysis','FydeOS for PC 17.1 R114, FydeOS for VMware 17.0 R114, FydeOS for You 17.1 R114, and OpenFyde R114 were discovered to be configured with the root password saved as a wildcard. This allows attackers to gain root access without a password.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'','',4),('CVE-2024-25830','2024-02-29','2025-06-10','Analyzed','F-logic DataCube3 v1.0 is vulnerable to Incorrect Access Control due to an improper directory access restriction. An unauthenticated, remote attacker can exploit this, by sending a URI that contains the path of the configuration file. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to extract the root and admin password.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'f-logic','datacube3_firmware, datacube3',2),('CVE-2024-25832','2024-02-29','2025-03-27','Modified','F-logic DataCube3 v1.0 is vulnerable to unrestricted file upload, which could allow an authenticated malicious actor to upload a file of dangerous type by manipulating the filename extension.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'f-logic','datacube3',2),('CVE-2024-2583