INSERT INTO `CVE_2024` VALUES ('CVE-2024-2624','2024-06-06','2024-11-21','Modified','A path traversal and arbitrary file upload vulnerability exists in the parisneo/lollms-webui application, specifically within the `@router.get(\"/switch_personal_path\")` endpoint in `./lollms-webui/lollms_core/lollms/server/endpoints/lollms_user.py`. The vulnerability arises due to insufficient sanitization of user-supplied input for the `path` parameter, allowing an attacker to specify arbitrary file system paths. This flaw enables direct arbitrary file uploads, leakage of `personal_data`, and overwriting of configurations in `lollms-webui`->`configs` by exploiting the same named directory in `personal_data`. The issue affects the latest version of the application and is fixed in version 9.4. Successful exploitation could lead to sensitive information disclosure, unauthorized file uploads, and potentially remote code execution by overwriting critical configuration files.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'lollms','lollms_web_ui',4),('CVE-2024-26240','2024-04-09','2025-01-08','Analyzed','Secure Boot Security Feature Bypass Vulnerability',8.0,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.1,'microsoft','windows_server_2022, windows_11_23h2, windows_10_22h2, windows_10_1809, windows_10_1507',2),('CVE-2024-26241','2024-04-09','2025-01-08','Analyzed','Win32k Elevation of Privilege Vulnerability',7.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.8,'microsoft','windows_server_2022, windows_11_23h2, windows_10_1809, windows_10_1507, windows_server_2019',2),('CVE-2024-26242','2024-04-09','2025-01-08','Analyzed','Windows Telephony Server Elevation of Privilege Vulnerability',7.0,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.0,'microsoft','windows_server_2022, windows_11_23h2, windows_10_22h2, windows_10_1809, windows_10_1507',2),('CVE-2024-26243','2024-04-09','2025-01-08','Analyzed','Windows USB Print Driver Elevation of Privilege Vulnerability',7.0,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.0,'microsoft','windows_server_2022, windows_11_23h2, windows_10_22h2, windows_server_2022_23h2, windows_11_22h2',2),('CVE-2024-26244','2024-04-09','2024-12-06','Analyzed','Microsoft WDAC OLE DB provider for SQL Server Remote Code Execution Vulnerability',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'microsoft','windows_server_2022, windows_11_23h2, windows_10_22h2, windows_10_1809, windows_10_1507',2),('CVE-2024-26245','2024-04-09','2025-01-08','Analyzed','Windows SMB Elevation of Privilege Vulnerability',7.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.8,'microsoft','windows_10_1507',2),('CVE-2024-26248','2024-04-09','2025-01-08','Analyzed','Windows Kerberos Elevation of Privilege Vulnerability',7.5,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.6,'microsoft','windows_server_2022, windows_11_23h2, windows_10_22h2, windows_10_1809, windows_10_1507',2),('CVE-2024-2625','2024-03-20','2024-11-21','Modified','Object lifecycle issue in V8 in Google Chrome prior to 123.0.6312.58 allowed a remote attacker to potentially exploit object corruption via a crafted HTML page. (Chromium security severity: High)',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'google, fedoraproject','chrome, fedora',10),('CVE-2024-26254','2024-04-09','2024-12-05','Analyzed','Microsoft Virtual Machine Bus (VMBus) Denial of Service Vulnerability',7.5,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H',3.6,3.9,'microsoft','windows_server_2022, windows_11_23h2, windows_10_1809, windows_10_22h2, windows_server_2019',2),('CVE-2024-26256','2024-04-09','2025-01-08','Analyzed','Libarchive Remote Code Execution Vulnerability',7.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.8,'libarchive, microsoft, fedoraproject','windows_11_23h2, windows_server_2022_23h2, windows_11_22h2, fedora, libarchive',10),('CVE-2024-26257','2024-04-09','2024-12-05','Analyzed','Microsoft Excel Remote Code Execution Vulnerability',7.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.8,'microsoft','365_apps, office',2),('CVE-2024-26258','2024-04-04','2024-11-26','Awaiting Analysis','OS command injection vulnerability in ELECOM wireless LAN routers allows a network-adjacent attacker with credentials to execute arbitrary OS commands by sending a specially crafted request to the product.',7.1,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.2,'','',4),('CVE-2024-26260','2024-02-15','2025-01-23','Analyzed','The functionality for synchronization in HGiga OAKlouds\' certain moudules has an OS Command Injection vulnerability, allowing remote attackers to inject system commands within specific request parameters. This enables the execution of arbitrary code on the remote server without permission.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'hgiga','oaklouds-organization-3.0, oaklouds-webbase-3.0, oaklouds-organization-2.0, oaklouds-webbase-2.0',4),('CVE-2024-26261','2024-02-15','2025-01-23','Analyzed','The functionality for file download in HGiga OAKlouds\' certain modules contains an Arbitrary File Read and Delete vulnerability. Attackers can put file path in specific request parameters, allowing them to download the file without login. Furthermore, the file will be deleted after being downloaded.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'hgiga','oaklouds-organization-3.0, oaklouds-webbase-3.0, oaklouds-organization-2.0, oaklouds-webbase-2.0',4),('CVE-2024-26262','2024-02-15','2025-01-23','Analyzed','EBM Technologies Uniweb/SoliPACS WebServer\'s query functionality lacks proper restrictions of user input, allowing remote attackers authenticated as regular user to inject SQL commands for reading, modifying, and deleting database records, as well as executing system commands. Attackers may even leverage the dbo privilege in the database for privilege escalation, elevating their privileges to administrator .',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'ebmtech','uniweb/solipacs_webserver',2),('CVE-2024-26264','2024-02-15','2025-01-23','Analyzed','EBM Technologies RISWEB\'s specific query function parameter does not properly restrict user input, and this feature page is accessible without login. This allows remote attackers to inject SQL commands without authentication, enabling them to read, modify, and delete database records.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'ebmtech','risweb',2),('CVE-2024-26266','2024-02-21','2025-01-28','Analyzed','Multiple stored cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities in Liferay Portal 7.2.0 through 7.4.3.13, and older unsupported versions, and Liferay DXP 7.4 before update 10, 7.3 before update 4, 7.2 before fix pack 17, and older unsupported versions allow remote authenticated users to inject arbitrary web script or HTML via a crafted payload injected into the first/middle/last name text field of the user who creates an entry in the (1) Announcement widget, or (2) Alerts widget.',9.0,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H',6.0,2.3,'liferay','liferay_portal, digital_experience_platform',2),('CVE-2024-26269','2024-02-21','2025-01-28','Analyzed','Cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability in the Frontend JS module\'s portlet.js in Liferay Portal 7.2.0 through 7.4.3.37, and Liferay DXP 7.4 before update 38, 7.3 before update 11, 7.2 before fix pack 20, and older unsupported versions allows remote attackers to inject arbitrary web script or HTML via the anchor (hash) part of a URL.',9.6,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H',6.0,2.8,'liferay','liferay_portal, digital_experience_platform',2),('CVE-2024-2627','2024-03-20','2024-11-21','Modified','Use after free in Canvas in Google Chrome prior to 123.0.6312.58 allowed a remote attacker to potentially exploit heap corruption via a crafted HTML page. (Chromium security severity: Medium)',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'google, fedoraproject','chrome, fedora',10),('CVE-2024-26271','2024-10-22','2024-12-10','Analyzed','Cross-site request forgery (CSRF) vulnerability in the My Account widget in Liferay Portal 7.4.3.75 through 7.4.3.111, and Liferay DXP 2023.Q4.0 through 2023.Q4.2, 2023.Q3.1 through 2023.Q3.5, 7.4 update 75 through update 92 and 7.3 update 32 through update 36 allows remote attackers to (1) change user passwords, (2) shut down the server, (3) execute arbitrary code in the scripting console, (4) and perform other administrative actions via the _com_liferay_my_account_web_portlet_MyAccountPortlet_backURL parameter.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'liferay','digital_experience_platform, liferay_portal',1),('CVE-2024-26272','2024-10-22','2024-12-10','Analyzed','Cross-site request forgery (CSRF) vulnerability in the content page editor in Liferay Portal 7.3.2 through 7.4.3.107, and Liferay DXP 2023.Q4.0 through 2023.Q4.2, 2023.Q3.1 through 2023.Q3.5, 7.4 GA through update 92 and 7.3 GA through update 35 allows remote attackers to (1) change user passwords, (2) shut down the server, (3) execute arbitrary code in the scripting console, (4) and perform other administrative actions via the p_l_back_url parameter.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'liferay','digital_experience_platform, liferay_portal',1),('CVE-2024-26273','2024-10-22','2024-12-10','Analyzed','Cross-site request forgery (CSRF) vulnerability in the content page editor in Liferay Portal 7.4.0 through 7.4.3.103, and Liferay DXP 2023.Q4.0 through 2023.Q4.2, 2023.Q3.1 through 2023.Q3.5, 7.4 GA through update 92 and 7.3 update 29 through update 35 allows remote attackers to (1) change user passwords, (2) shut down the server, (3) execute arbitrary code in the scripting console, (4) and perform other administrative actions via the _com_liferay_commerce_catalog_web_internal_portlet_CommerceCatalogsPortlet_redirect parameter.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'liferay','digital_experience_platform, liferay_portal',1),('CVE-2024-26275','2024-04-09','2024-11-21','Awaiting Analysis','A vulnerability has been identified in JT2Go (All versions < V2312.0004), Parasolid V35.1 (All versions < V35.1.254), Parasolid V36.0 (All versions < V36.0.207), Parasolid V36.1 (All versions < V36.1.147), Teamcenter Visualization V14.2 (All versions < V14.2.0.12), Teamcenter Visualization V14.3 (All versions < V14.3.0.9), Teamcenter Visualization V2312 (All versions < V2312.0004). The affected applications contain an out of bounds read past the end of an allocated structure while parsing specially crafted X_T files. This could allow an attacker to execute code in the context of the current process.',7.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.8,'','',4),('CVE-2024-26282','2024-02-22','2025-03-27','Analyzed','Using an AMP url with a canonical element, an attacker could have executed JavaScript from an opened bookmarked page. This vulnerability affects Firefox for iOS < 123.',7.1,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:H/A:N',4.2,2.8,'mozilla','firefox',4),('CVE-2024-26283','2024-02-22','2025-03-27','Analyzed','An attacker could have executed unauthorized scripts on top origin sites using a JavaScript URI when opening an external URL with a custom Firefox scheme. This vulnerability affects Firefox for iOS < 123.',7.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.8,'mozilla','firefox',4),('CVE-2024-26288','2024-03-12','2025-01-23','Analyzed','An unauthenticated remote attacker can influence the communication due to the lack of encryption of sensitive data via a MITM. Charging is not affected.',8.7,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:N',5.8,2.2,'phoenixcontact','charx_sec-3050, charx_sec-3000, charx_sec-3050_firmware, charx_sec-3000_firmware, charx_sec-3100_firmware',2),('CVE-2024-26289','2024-05-27','2025-04-04','Analyzed','Deserialization of Untrusted Data vulnerability in PMB Services PMB allows Remote Code Inclusion.This issue affects PMB: from 7.5.1 before 7.5.6-2, from 7.4.1 before 7.4.9, from 7.3.1 before 7.3.18.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'sigb','pmb',4),('CVE-2024-26294','2024-02-27','2025-03-27','Analyzed','Vulnerabilities in the ClearPass Policy Manager web-based management interface allow remote authenticated users to run arbitrary commands on the underlying host. A successful exploit could allow an attacker to execute arbitrary commands as root on the underlying operating system leading to complete system compromise.  ',7.2,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.2,'arubanetworks','clearpass_policy_manager',2),('CVE-2024-26295','2024-02-27','2025-03-27','Analyzed','Vulnerabilities in the ClearPass Policy Manager web-based management interface allow remote authenticated users to run arbitrary commands on the underlying host. A successful exploit could allow an attacker to execute arbitrary commands as root on the underlying operating system leading to complete system compromise.  ',7.2,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.2,'arubanetworks','clearpass_policy_manager',2),('CVE-2024-26296','2024-02-27','2025-03-27','Analyzed','Vulnerabilities in the ClearPass Policy Manager web-based management interface allow remote authenticated users to run arbitrary commands on the underlying host. A successful exploit could allow an attacker to execute arbitrary commands as root on the underlying operating system leading to complete system compromise.  ',7.2,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.2,'arubanetworks','clearpass_policy_manager',2),('CVE-2024-26297','2024-02-27','2025-03-27','Analyzed','Vulnerabilities in the ClearPass Policy Manager web-based management interface allow remote authenticated users to run arbitrary commands on the underlying host. A successful exploit could allow an attacker to execute arbitrary commands as root on the underlying operating system leading to complete system compromise.  ',7.2,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.2,'arubanetworks','clearpass_policy_manager',2),('CVE-2024-26298','2024-02-27','2025-03-27','Analyzed','Vulnerabilities in the ClearPass Policy Manager web-based management interface allow remote authenticated users to run arbitrary commands on the underlying host. A successful exploit could allow an attacker to execute arbitrary commands as root on the underlying operating system leading to complete system compromise.  ',7.2,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.2,'arubanetworks','clearpass_policy_manager',2),('CVE-2024-26304','2024-05-01','2024-11-21','Awaiting Analysis','There is a buffer overflow vulnerability in the underlying L2/L3 Management service that could lead to unauthenticated remote code execution by sending specially crafted packets destined to the PAPI (Aruba\'s access point management protocol) UDP port (8211). Successful exploitation of this vulnerability results in the ability to execute arbitrary code as a privileged user on the underlying operating system.   ',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'','',2),('CVE-2024-26305','2024-05-01','2024-11-21','Awaiting Analysis','There is a buffer overflow vulnerability in the underlying Utility daemon that could lead to unauthenticated remote code execution by sending specially crafted packets destined to the PAPI (Aruba\'s access point management protocol) UDP port (8211). Successful exploitation of this vulnerability results in the ability