'CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.1,'','',6),('CVE-2024-31822','2024-04-29','2024-11-21','Awaiting Analysis','An issue in Ecommerce-CodeIgniter-Bootstrap commit v. d22b54e8915f167a135046ceb857caaf8479c4da allows a remote attacker to execute arbitrary code via the saveLanguageFiles method of the Languages.php component.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'','',6),('CVE-2024-31823','2024-04-29','2024-11-21','Awaiting Analysis','An issue in Ecommerce-CodeIgniter-Bootstrap commit v. d22b54e8915f167a135046ceb857caaf8479c4da allows a remote attacker to execute arbitrary code via the removeSecondaryImage method of the Publish.php component.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'','',6),('CVE-2024-3183','2024-06-12','2024-11-21','Modified','A vulnerability was found in FreeIPA in a way when a Kerberos TGS-REQ is encrypted using the client’s session key. This key is different for each new session, which protects it from brute force attacks. However, the ticket it contains is encrypted using the target principal key directly. For user principals, this key is a hash of a public per-principal randomly-generated salt and the user’s password.  If a principal is compromised it means the attacker would be able to retrieve tickets encrypted to any principal, all of them being encrypted by their own key directly. By taking these tickets and salts offline, the attacker could run brute force attacks to find character strings able to decrypt tickets when combined to a principal salt (i.e. find the principal’s password).',8.1,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N',5.2,2.8,'redhat','enterprise_linux, enterprise_linux_eus, enterprise_linux_update_services_for_sap_solutions, enterprise_linux_aus, enterprise_linux_tus',25),('CVE-2024-31837','2024-04-30','2024-11-21','Awaiting Analysis','DMitry (Deepmagic Information Gathering Tool) 1.3a has a format-string vulnerability, with a threat model similar to CVE-2017-7938.',8.4,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.5,'','',2),('CVE-2024-31841','2024-04-19','2025-05-21','Analyzed','An issue was discovered in Italtel Embrace 1.6.4. The web server fails to sanitize input data, allowing remote unauthenticated attackers to read arbitrary files on the filesystem.',7.5,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N',3.6,3.9,'italtel','embrace',2),('CVE-2024-31842','2024-08-20','2024-10-29','Modified','An issue was discovered in Italtel Embrace 1.6.4. The web application inserts the access token of an authenticated user inside GET requests. The query string for the URL could be saved in the browser\'s history, passed through Referers to other web sites, stored in web logs, or otherwise recorded in other sources. If the query string contains sensitive information such as session identifiers, then attackers can use this information to launch further attacks. Because the access token in sent in GET requests, this vulnerability could lead to complete account takeover.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'italtel','embrace',1),('CVE-2024-31846','2024-04-19','2025-05-21','Analyzed','An issue was discovered in Italtel Embrace 1.6.4. The web application does not restrict or incorrectly restricts access to a resource from an unauthorized actor.',7.5,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N',3.6,3.9,'italtel','embrace',2),('CVE-2024-31848','2024-04-05','2024-11-21','Awaiting Analysis','A path traversal vulnerability exists in the Java version of CData API Server < 23.4.8844 when running using the embedded Jetty server, which could allow an unauthenticated remote attacker to gain complete administrative access to the application.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'','',2),('CVE-2024-31849','2024-04-05','2024-11-21','Awaiting Analysis','A path traversal vulnerability exists in the Java version of CData Connect < 23.4.8846 when running using the embedded Jetty server, which could allow an unauthenticated remote attacker to gain complete administrative access to the application.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'','',2),('CVE-2024-31850','2024-04-05','2024-11-21','Awaiting Analysis','A path traversal vulnerability exists in the Java version of CData Arc < 23.4.8839 when running using the embedded Jetty server, which could allow an unauthenticated remote attacker to gain access to sensitive information and perform limited actions.',8.6,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:L',4.7,3.9,'','',2),('CVE-2024-31851','2024-04-05','2024-11-21','Awaiting Analysis','A path traversal vulnerability exists in the Java version of CData Sync < 23.4.8843 when running using the embedded Jetty server, which could allow an unauthenticated remote attacker to gain access to sensitive information and perform limited actions.',8.6,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:L',4.7,3.9,'','',2),('CVE-2024-31853','2025-07-08','2025-08-20','Analyzed','A vulnerability has been identified in SICAM TOOLBOX II (All versions < V07.11). During establishment of a https connection to the TLS server of a managed device, the affected application doesn\'t check the extended key usage attribute of that device\'s certificate. This could allow an attacker to execute an on-path network (MitM) attack.',8.1,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.2,'siemens','sicam_toolbox_ii',1),('CVE-2024-31854','2025-07-08','2025-08-20','Analyzed','A vulnerability has been identified in SICAM TOOLBOX II (All versions < V07.11). During establishment of a https connection to the TLS server of a managed device, the affected application doesn\'t check device\'s certificate common name against an expected value. This could allow an attacker to execute an on-path network (MitM) attack.',8.1,