ically, the application fails to validate or format JSON data sent in an HTTP POST request to `/api/workspace/:workspace-slug/update`, allowing it to be executed as part of a database query without restrictions. This flaw enables users with a manager role to craft a request that includes nested write operations, effectively allowing them to create new Administrator accounts.',7.2,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.2,'mintplexlabs','anythingllm',4),('CVE-2024-42885','2024-09-05','2025-07-03','Analyzed','SQL Injection vulnerability in ESAFENET CDG 5.6 and before allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code via the id parameter of the data.jsp page.',9.1,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N',5.2,3.9,'esafenet','cdg',1),('CVE-2024-4290','2024-05-21','2025-05-21','Analyzed','The Sailthru Triggermail WordPress plugin through 1.1 does not sanitise and escape some of its settings, which could allow high privilege users such as admin to perform Stored Cross-Site Scripting attacks even when the unfiltered_html capability is disallowed (for example in multisite setup)',7.1,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:L',3.7,2.8,'jontasc','sailthru_triggermail',2),('CVE-2024-42902','2024-09-03','2025-07-03','Analyzed','An issue in the js_localize.php function of LimeSurvey v6.6.2 and before allows attackers to execute arbitrary code via injecting a crafted payload into the lng parameter of the js_localize.php function',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'limesurvey','limesurvey',3),('CVE-2024-42905','2024-08-28','2024-08-29','Awaiting Analysis','Beijing Digital China Cloud Technology Co., Ltd. DCME-320 v.7.4.12.60 has a command execution vulnerability, which can be exploited to obtain device administrator privileges via the getVar function in the code/function/system/tool/ping.php file.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'','',