d even when still in use.  The first scenario occurs where a record header has been received from the network and processed by OpenSSL, but the full record body has not yet arrive',7.5,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H',3.6,3.9,'','',6),('CVE-2024-47410','2024-10-09','2024-10-10','Analyzed','Animate versions 23.0.7, 24.0.4 and earlier are affected by a Stack-based Buffer Overflow vulnerability that could result in arbitrary code execution in the context of the current user. Exploitation of this issue requires user interaction in that a victim must open a malicious file.',7.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.8,'apple, adobe, microsoft','windows, animate, macos',1),('CVE-2024-47411','2024-10-09','2024-10-10','Analyzed','Animate versions 23.0.7, 24.0.4 and earlier are affected by an Access of Uninitialized Pointer vulnerability that could result in arbitrary code execution in the context of the current user. Exploitation of this issue requires user interaction in that a victim must open a malicious file.',7.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.8,'apple, adobe, microsoft','windows, animate, macos',1),('CVE-2024-47412','2024-10-09','2024-10-10','Analyzed','Animate versions 23.0.7, 24.0.4 and earlier are affected by a Use After Free vulnerability that could result in arbitrary code execution in the context of the current user. Exploitation of this issue requires user interaction in that a victim must open a malicious file.',7.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,1.8,'apple, adobe, microsoft','windows, animate, macos',1),('CVE-2024-47413','2024-10-09','2024-10-10','Analyzed','Animate versions 23.0.7, 24.0.4 and earlier are affected by a Use After Free vulnerability that could result in arbitrary code execution in the context of the current user. Exploitation of this issue requires user interaction in that a victim must open a malicious file.',7.8,'HIGH'