2),('CVE-2024-51329','2024-11-04','2024-11-06','Analyzed','A Host header injection vulnerability in Agile-Board 1.0 allows attackers to obtain the password reset token via user interaction with a crafted password reset link.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'idrsdev','agile-board',2),('CVE-2024-5133','2024-06-06','2024-11-21','Modified','In lunary-ai/lunary version 1.2.4, an account takeover vulnerability exists due to the exposure of password recovery tokens in API responses. Specifically, when a user initiates the password reset process, the recovery token is included in the response of the `GET /v1/users/me/org` endpoint, which lists all users in a team. This allows any authenticated user to capture the recovery token of another user and subsequently change that user\'s password without consent, effectively taking over the account. The issue lies in the inclusion of the `recovery_token` attribute in the users object returned by the API.',8.1,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N',5.2,2.8,'lunary','lunary',2),('CVE-2024-5135','2024-05-20','2025-02-21','Analyzed','A vulnerability was found in PHPGurukul Directory Management System 1.0. It has been rated as critical. This issue affects some unknown processing of the file /admin/index.php. The manipulation of the argument username leads to sql injection. The attack may be initiated remotely. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. The associated identifier of this vulnerability is VDB-265211.',7.3,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L',3.4,3.9,'phpgurukul','directory_management_system',8),('CVE-2024-51358','2024-11-05','2024-11-07','Awaiting Analysis','An issue in Linux Server Heimdall v.2.6.1 allows a remote attacker to execute arbitrary code via a crafted script to the Add new application.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'','',1),('CVE-2024-51360','2025-05-23','2025-05-29','Modified','An issue in Hospital Management System In PHP V4.0 allows a remote attacker to execute arbitrary code via the hms/doctor/edit-profile.php file',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'phpgurukul','hospital_management_system',1),('CVE-2024-51363','2024-12-03','2024-12-11','Awaiting Analysis','Insecure deserialization in Hodoku v2.3.0 to v2.3.2 allows attackers to execute arbitrary code.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'','',1),('CVE-2024-51364','2024-11-21','2024-11-27','Awaiting Analysis','An arbitrary file upload vulnerability in ModbusMechanic v3.0 allows attackers to execute arbitrary code via uploading a crafted .xml file.',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'','',2),('CVE-2024-51366','2024-11-21','2024-12-04','Awaiting Analysis','An arbitrary file upload vulnerability in the component RoamingOmega of OmegaT v6.0.1 allows attackers to execute arbitrary code via uploading a crafted .conf file.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'','',3),('CVE-2024-51367','2024-11-21','2024-11-27','Awaiting Analysis','An arbitrary file upload vulnerability in the component Usersusername.BlackBoard of BlackBoard v2.0.0.2 allows attackers to execute arbitrary code via uploading a crafted .xml file.',9.8,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,3.9,'','',2),('CVE-2024-51376','2025-02-12','2025-02-13','Awaiting Analysis','Directory Traversal vulnerability in yeqifu carRental v.1.0 allows a remote attacker to obtain sensitive information via the file/downloadFile.action?path= component.',7.5,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N',3.6,3.9,'','',2),('CVE-2024-51378','2024-10-29','2025-07-30','Analyzed','getresetstatus in dns/views.py and ftp/views.py in CyberPanel (aka Cyber Panel) before 1c0c6cb allows remote attackers to bypass authentication and execute arbitrary commands via /dns/getresetstatus or /ftp/getresetstatus by bypassing secMiddleware (which is only for a POST request) and using shell metacharacters in the statusfile property, as exploited in the wild in October 2024 by PSAUX. Versions through 2.3.6 and (unpatched) 2.3.7 are affected.',10.0,'CRITICAL','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H',6.0,3.9,'cyberpanel','cyberpanel',7),('CVE-2024-51379','2024-11-05','2025-06-24','Analyzed','Stored Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability discovered in JATOS v3.9.3. The vulnerability exists in the description component of the study section, where an attacker can inject JavaScript into the description field. This allows for the execution of malicious scripts when an admin views the description, potentially leading to account takeover and unauthorized actions.',8.4,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H',6.0,1.7,'jatos','jatos',1),('CVE-2024-5138','2024-05-31','2024-11-21','Awaiting Analysis','The snapctl component within snapd allows a confined snap to interact with the snapd daemon to take certain privileged actions on behalf of the snap. It was found that snapctl did not properly parse command-line arguments, allowing an unprivileged user to trigger an authorised action on behalf of the snap that would normally require administrator privileges to perform. This could possibly allow an unprivileged user to perform a denial of service or similar.',8.1,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H',5.2,2.8,'','',8),('CVE-2024-51380','2024-11-05','2025-06-24','Analyzed','Stored Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability discovered in the Properties Component of JATOS v3.9.3. This flaw allows an attacker to inject malicious JavaScript into the properties section of a study, specifically within the UUID field. When an admin user accesses the study\'s properties, the injected script is executed in the admin\'s browser, which could lead to unauthorized actions, including account compromise and privilege escalation.',8.4,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H',6.0,1.7,'jatos','jatos',1),('CVE-2024-51381','2024-11-05','2025-06-24','Analyzed','Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) vulnerability in JATOS v3.9.3 that allows attackers to perform actions reserved for administrators, including creating admin accounts. This critical flaw can lead to unauthorized activities, compromising the security and integrity of the platform, especially if an attacker gains administrative control.',8.4,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H',6.0,1.7,'jatos','jatos',1),('CVE-2024-51382','2024-11-05','2025-06-24','Analyzed','Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) vulnerability in JATOS v3.9.3 allows an attacker to reset the administrator\'s password. This critical security flaw can result in unauthorized access to the platform, enabling attackers to hijack admin accounts and compromise the integrity and security of the system.',8.4,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H',6.0,1.7,'jatos','jatos',1),('CVE-2024-51392','2025-05-29','2025-05-30','Awaiting Analysis','An issue in OpenKnowledgeMaps Headstart v7 allows a remote attacker to escalate privileges via the url parameter of the getPDF.php component',8.8,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H',5.9,2.8,'','',2),('CVE-2024-51408','2024-11-04','2024-11-06','Analyzed','AppSmith Community 1.8.3 before 1.46 allows SSRF via New DataSource for application/json requests to 169.254.169.254 to retrieve AWS metadata credentials.',8.5,'HIGH','v3.1','CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H',6.0,1.8,'appsmith','appsmith',3),('CVE-2024-51424','2024-10-30','2024-11-04','Awaiting Analysis','An issue in the PepeGxng smart contract (which can be run on the Ethereum blockchain) allows remote attackers to have an unspecified impact via the Owned.setOwner function. NOTE: this is disputed by third parties because the impact is limited to function calls.',